# __PACKAGE_NAME__

GENERATED npm package candidate — do not hand-edit. Regenerate via `python3 compiler/tools/regen_all.py` in the DeliberateCode/System2 repo.

System2 is a deliberate-reasoning workflow for the [Pi coding agent](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi). This candidate contains the compiler-generated base workflow, prompts, and bounded safety extension. It has no install scripts or bundled runtime dependencies; Pi provides the declared host peer.

Native acceptance is pinned to **Pi 0.85.1**. It covers package command discovery, Orchestrator-first public RPC/SDK startup, branch-local workflow restoration, human status, subprocess contracts for all 13 roles, and a real Pi JSON-mode child executing the terminating structured completion tool through a deterministic test provider. It also covers bounded dangerous-command/sensitive-path blocks, structured off-scope writes, and benign negative controls. Hermetic subprocess doubles exercise failure and all-role invocation paths without external model traffic; they are not native CLI acceptance. This is evidence for the tested version, not a compatibility claim for untested Pi versions.

The `"*"` peer range follows Pi's package guidance for host-provided core imports; it is a loader convention, not a claim of validation against every Pi version.

## Availability

This package is **pending publication**. There is no supported npm installation command, and the package name must not be treated as currently installable.

## Materialize project files

After publication, the package-discovered `/system2-init` command will materialize `.pi/SYSTEM.md` and `system2.pi.lock.json` into the current project, then reload Pi so resources are rediscovered. It does not materialize or replace caller-owned `AGENTS.md`. Re-running is idempotent: byte-identical managed files are skipped, locally modified managed files are left untouched unless `--force` is supplied, lexical/symlink escapes are refused, writes use atomic replacement, and unmanaged files are never touched.

## Scope

The candidate contains the **base 13-role workflow** composed with an empty overlay set. The parent remains the Orchestrator. `system2_delegate` starts an ephemeral Pi subprocess with role-specific prompt/tools and no recursive delegation tool, then returns one bounded report. `/delegate` is only a human convenience request to the parent; it never switches parent authority. Process, Pi-session, and model-context isolation are provided; filesystem and inherited-credential isolation are not. CLI sessions reuse Pi's resolved absolute entry; SDK hosts must set `SYSTEM2_PI_BIN` to an absolute owner-trusted, non-group/world-writable Pi executable. There is no bare `pi` `PATH` fallback. Ambient extensions are disabled in children, so models registered only by a custom-provider extension are unavailable and delegation fails closed.

Overlays and profiles are not end-user package UX. Applying them requires the source compiler; the published package will contain no compiler and will read no overlay input at install time or runtime.

## Enforcement fidelity

The package-discovered Pi extension registers `tool_call` handlers that block declared dangerous-command patterns, sensitive structured paths/ordinary literal shell tokens, structured off-lease writes, and supported off-lease shell redirection/`tee` targets before execution. The parent active tool set excludes bash/write/edit and its safety handler blocks them if re-enabled. A child target must match both its canonical role scope and delegated task scope. Lease enforcement is adapted/partial, not a general shell-write parser: commands such as `touch`, `cp`, `mv`, `install`, `sed -i`, interpreters, and build tools are unsupported. Dangerous-command matching does not claim arbitrary-shell normalization, and sensitive-token matching does not expand shell expressions. Malformed or overflowing supported extraction fails closed; unknown custom tool schemas are outside the sensitive-path claim.

Budget is advisory: the completion schema bounds and contract-checks specialist-reported file/line totals, but it does not compute them from the repository diff. Formatting and type-checking are also advisory. Task scopes and artifact-input digests must be present in the latest human gate approval. Invalid/interrupted workflow state blocks mutation and delegation until explicit human recovery; an extension upgrade changes the provenance digest and therefore also requires recovery of an in-progress workflow. See `system2.pi.lock.json` for the per-capability report.

